theorem a-label-given-again-inside-a-block
  note        The block inside labels its assumption J, as the block around it
              does. Once it closes, J is the outer block's again: x > 0, not
              y > 0.
  then for all x ∈ ℝ, if x > 0 then x ≥ 0 and x + 1 > 0

1.  For all x ∈ ℝ, if x > 0 then x ≥ 0 and x + 1 > 0.
    proof
    let x ∈ ℝ                                                         (K1)
    assume x > 0                                                      (J)

    1.1.  For all y ∈ ℝ, if y > 0 then y + 1 > 0.
          proof
          let y ∈ ℝ                                                   (K2)
          assume y > 0                                                (J)

          1.1.1.  y + 1 > 1
                  inequalities
                    y > 0            J
                    y + 1 > 1        adding 1

          1.1.2.  1 > 0
                  arithmetic

          1.1.3.  y + 1 > 0
                  transitivity, from 1.1.1, 1.1.2

    1.2.  x + 1 > 0
          instantiate y := x in line 1.1, from J

    1.3.  x ≥ 0
          inequalities
            x > 0            J
            x ≥ 0            weakening

    1.4.  x ≥ 0 and x + 1 > 0
          join 1.3, 1.2
